✅ What is GOT?
→ a table storing addresses of library functions

✅ Why is GOT useful for exploitation?
→ writable when No RELRO
→ overwrite entry → redirect function call

✅ What did we do?
→ overwrote exit@GOT with o() address
→ program calls exit() → jumps to o() instead → shell

✅ Why not buffer overflow here?
→ no return address to overwrite
→ exit() called directly after printf

✅ What is PLT?
→ Procedure Linkage Table
→ the bridge between your code and library functions
→ program calls exit@plt → PLT looks up GOT → jumps there